%description:
ARP Probe handling: an ARP request whose sender protocol address is all zeroes is a legal
RFC 5227 ARP Probe and must be processed like any other ARP request.

Two StandardHosts on an Ethernet link. At t=1s a trigger module calls INET's own
Arp::sendArpProbe(ie, ie->getMacAddress(), <host2's address>) on host1's ARP module -- the
RFC 5227 probe builder, which sets srcIpAddress to Ipv4Address::UNSPECIFIED_ADDRESS. The
frame is broadcast on the real link and reaches host2's ARP module through the normal
dispatcher path; no INET source is modified and the packet is built by INET code.

Clauses: RFC 5227 section 2.1.1 defines the ARP Probe as an ARP request with an all-zero
'sender IP address' field, sent to check whether an address is already in use. Section 2.5
requires the address owner to answer it: "a host ... MUST respond to conflicting ARP
Probes ... to defend its address". host2 owns the probed address, so it must send an
ARP reply and the run must complete normally.

Finding IPV4-087. Arp::processArpPacket() rejects an unspecified sender address with
`throw cRuntimeError("wrong ARP packet: source IPv4 address is empty")`, which kills the
whole simulation instead of dropping or answering the frame. Any peer that sends a probe --
INET's own sendArpProbe(), a hand-written model, or an emulated external host -- takes the
simulation down; sendArpProbe() currently has no caller in the tree, which is the only
reason INET does not do this to itself today.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: ArpProbeTrigger.ned

simple ArpProbeTrigger
{
    parameters:
        @display("i=block/control");
}

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: ArpProbeTrigger.cc

#include "inet/networklayer/arp/ipv4/Arp.h"
#include "inet/networklayer/common/NetworkInterface.h"
#include "inet/networklayer/common/InterfaceTable.h"
#include "inet/networklayer/common/L3AddressResolver.h"

namespace @TESTNAME@ {

using namespace inet;

class INET_API ArpProbeTrigger : public cSimpleModule
{
  protected:
    virtual void initialize() override { scheduleAt(SimTime(1, SIMTIME_S), new cMessage("trigger")); }
    virtual void handleMessage(cMessage *msg) override;
};

Define_Module(ArpProbeTrigger);

void ArpProbeTrigger::handleMessage(cMessage *msg)
{
    delete msg;

    auto *arp = check_and_cast<Arp *>(getModuleByPath("^.host1.ipv4.arp"));
    auto *ift = check_and_cast<IInterfaceTable *>(getModuleByPath("^.host1.interfaceTable"));
    NetworkInterface *ie = ift->findInterfaceByName("eth0");
    if (ie == nullptr)
        throw cRuntimeError("eth0 not found on host1");

    Ipv4Address probedAddr = L3AddressResolver().addressOf(getModuleByPath("^.host2")).toIpv4();
    EV_INFO << "TRIGGER: sending ARP Probe for " << probedAddr << " from " << ie->getMacAddress() << endl;
    arp->sendArpProbe(ie, ie->getMacAddress(), probedAddr);
}

}

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: TestNetwork.ned

import inet.networklayer.configurator.ipv4.Ipv4NetworkConfigurator;
import inet.node.ethernet.Eth100M;
import inet.node.inet.StandardHost;

network TestNetwork
{
    submodules:
        configurator: Ipv4NetworkConfigurator;
        trigger: ArpProbeTrigger;
        host1: StandardHost;
        host2: StandardHost;
    connections:
        host1.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> host2.ethg++;
}

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../../src
network = TestNetwork
sim-time-limit = 5s
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-event-banners = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = "%C: "

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# RFC 5227 2.5: the owner of the probed address answers the probe
%contains: stdout
TestNetwork.host2.ipv4.arp: Sending (inet::Packet)arpREPLY
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# RFC 5227 2.1.1: an all-zero sender protocol address is legal, not an error
%not-contains: stderr
wrong ARP packet: source IPv4 address is empty
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%expected-failure: IPV4-087 -- Arp::processArpPacket() throws cRuntimeError("wrong ARP packet: source IPv4 address is empty") for an unspecified sender protocol address, so a legal RFC 5227 ARP Probe aborts the simulation instead of drawing a reply. Fails RFC 5227 2.1.1 and 2.5.
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
